<title>AUSTRIA: ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS MEN'S TWO-LEG DOWNHILL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS MEN'S TWO-LEG DOWNHILL.</headline>
<dateline>KITZBUEHEL, Austria 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Frenchman Luc Alphand won a men's Alpine ski World Cup two-leg downhill race on Friday, in a total time of two minutes 12.55 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Austria's Werner Franz finished second in 2:12.95 and William Besse of Switzerland was third with 2:13.13.</p>
